          "claim": "If $c=L$, step 2.2 gives tuned root factor $q=0$, which is minimal since root factors are nonnegative. If $c<L$, step 2.2 gives tuned interval factor $q$ and step 3.3 gives the lower bound $R\\ge q$ for every constant admissible pair, so the tuned parameters are minimax; step 5.1 gives the strict comparison with gradient descent, while step 3.2 records the repeated-root qualification.",
          "step": "6.1",
