          "claim": "For $t\\ge1$, factor the expression as $w_t=(-2)^t\\bigl(-\\tfrac35+\\tfrac85\\,16^{-t}\\bigr)$. Since $16^{-t}\\le1/16$, the term in parentheses is at most $-\\tfrac12$, hence $|w_t|\\ge2^{t-1}$. Induction gives $2^{t-1}\\ge t$ for $t\\ge1$. For any starting index $N\\ge1$ and any real $R>0$, put $B=\\max\\{N,R\\}$; since $\\mathbb R$ is a complete ordered field by [F3], [F4] supplies a natural number $t>B$, which we use under the usual embedding as an integer iteration index. Thus $t\\ge N$ and $|w_t|\\ge t>R$. Every tail is therefore unbounded. If the sequence converged to a real $\\ell$, some tail would satisfy $|w_t-\\ell|<1$ and hence $|w_t|<|\\ell|+1$, a contradiction.",
