        "notes": "Read the complete current Example and all three Verification steps, all four actual supplier sections and exact contract quotations, derivations and boundaries; reader/refuter findings are empty. Taking C=[1] supplies gradient x and 1+1/4-27/8=-17/8, so the recurrence polynomial is (r+2)(r+1/8). The explicit coefficients give w0=-3/5+8/5=1 and w1=6/5-1/5=1, and substitution plus induction establishes the formula. For t>=1 the bracket -3/5+(8/5)16^(-t)<=-1/2, giving |wt|>=2^(t-1)>=t; the latter induction starts at t=1 and doubles to dominate t+1. The Archimedean supplier applies to the complete real ordered field and yields a natural index beyond both N and R, proving every tail unbounded; a convergent real sequence has a tail bounded by |limit|+1. Initial indices 0 and 1, distinct negative roots and all large tails are covered. The infinite recurrence is the compatible continuation of every finite-horizon heavy-ball execution, with no new convergence assertion for the procedure. Explicit scalar data use no choice. No external empirical or nonquadratic claim is used, no defect or unmet prerequisite found, and no item edit is necessary."
