        "notes": "Reviewed after completing the level-1 theorem and unstable example. Read the complete current Example and all three Verification steps, all four cited supplier sections and current contract quotations/derivations/boundaries. A=diag(1,4,9) is real symmetric positive definite and has spectrum in [1,9], so the independently reviewed theorem applies with center zero, kappa=9, q=1/2 and alpha=beta=1/4. C=diag(1,2,3) gives C^T C=A and gradient Aw. Substitution gives polynomials (r-1/2)^2, r^2-r/4+1/4 and (r+1/2)^2; the middle roots 1/8 +/- i sqrt(15)/8 have squared modulus 16/64=1/4. Both endpoint repetitions are explicitly retained, so no pure q^t or one-step norm guarantee is inferred. Fixed-step GD with gamma=1/5 yields multipliers 4/5,1/5,-4/5 and worst factor 4/5. Initial w0=w1=(1,1,1) is admissible; no empty, zero-dimensional, choice or convergence issue is introduced. All exact supplier quotations match current source sections; reader/refuter findings are empty. No mathematical, citation, diagram or statement-link defect found; no repair or unmet prerequisite."
